<title>BRAZIL: Brazil lets Societe Generale buy bank.</title>
<headline>Brazil lets Societe Generale buy bank.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Monetary Council (CMN) Thursday authorized Societe Generale to buy out control of Brazilian bank Sogeral SA, officials said.</p>
<p>Societe Generale already owns 30 percent of voting shares and 20 percent of preferential shares in Sogeral but wants to increase its stake to 100 percent.</p>
<p>Central Bank officials said the CMN sent a resolution to President Fernando Henrique Cardoso to be signed.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358))</p>
